---
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import IndustryLayout from '@/layouts/IndustryLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What furniture springs do you make?',
    a: 'Torsion and extension springs for seating and fold mechanisms, plus small compression springs and wire-form clips, in 0.40–2.50 mm wire. Not zig-zag or heavy seating coils.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the spring be plated?',
    a: 'Yes, through partners. Say the finish on the drawing. We do not plate in-house.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the minimum order?',
    a: `Usually ${site.terms.moq}. Smaller development runs are charged.`,
  },
];
---

<IndustryLayout
  route="furniture"
  title="Furniture Spring Manufacturer in Pune"
  description="Torsion and extension springs for seating and fold mechanisms, wire Ø 0.40–2.50 mm. Made to drawing or sample in Talawade."
  h1="Furniture springs"
  lede="Torsion and extension springs for seating and fold mechanisms, in the 0.40–2.50 mm wire range. Not zig-zag upholstery coils."
  context="furniture springs"
  faqs={faqs}
  service={{ audience: 'Makers of seating and furniture mechanisms' }}
  related={[
    { to: 'torsion', label: 'Torsion springs', description: 'Folds, lids and ratchets.' },
    { to: 'extension', label: 'Tension / extension springs', description: 'Returns on a linkage.' },
    { to: 'wireForms', label: 'Wire forms', description: 'Clips and retainers.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Seating and fold mechanisms</h2>
  <p>
    Furniture is one of the industries we serve. In our unit that means{' '}
    <strong>torsion springs on a fold or a ratchet</strong>, extension springs on a return, and the
    odd compression spring or wire-form clip. It does not mean zig-zag sofa springs or anything
    above 2.50 mm wire.
  </p>
  <p>
    The spring is often visible, or it sits just under a cover, so finish and rust matter.
    Hard-drawn wire with a partner-applied finish is common. Stainless if the piece will live in a
    damp room.
  </p>

  <h2>What the drawing must say</h2>
  <p>
    For a torsion spring: wire, coil diameter, free angle, working angle, torque if you have it,
    both leg shapes, and wind direction. For an extension spring: wire, OD, length inside hooks,
    hook type, and a load at one working length.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have only the old spring, send an unused one. A furniture spring that has sat loaded for
    years has often taken set.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    Wire {site.capability.wireRangeLabel}. Usual minimum {site.terms.moq}. Quote within 24 hours.
    Dispatch ex-works Talawade. We supply across India.
  </p>
</IndustryLayout>
